# Environment Variables Template - Backend (Render)

## Required Variables

# Node Environment
NODE_ENV=production
PORT=3000

# Database (PostgreSQL from Render)
# Format: postgresql://username:password@host:5432/database
# Get this from Render Dashboard → Database → Info
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:5432/ecommerce_db

# JWT Authentication
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key-minimum-16-characters-long
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=your-refresh-secret-minimum-16-characters-long
JWT_EXPIRE=7d
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRE=30d

# CORS Configuration
# Update this with your Vercel frontend URL after deployment
CORS_ORIGIN=https://yourdomain.vercel.app

## Optional Variables (if using services)

# ImageKit (Image hosting & optimization)
IMAGEKIT_PUBLIC_KEY=your_public_key
IMAGEKIT_PRIVATE_KEY=your_private_key
IMAGEKIT_URL_ENDPOINT=https://ik.imagekit.io/yourspace/

# Redis Cache (for better performance)
# Format: redis://host:port or rediss://host:port (with TLS)
REDIS_URL=redis://host:port

# Logging
LOG_LEVEL=info
LOG_FILE=logs/app.log

# Rate Limiting
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW_MS=900000
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=500
AUTH_RATE_LIMIT_MAX=20

## How to Generate Secrets

# Method 1: Using Node.js
# node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"

# Method 2: Using OpenSSL
# openssl rand -hex 32

# Method 3: Online tool
# https://www.random.org/strings/

## Render Deploy Checklist

- [ ] Copy all required variables
- [ ] Generate secure JWT secrets (min 16 chars)
- [ ] Get DATABASE_URL from Render PostgreSQL
- [ ] Set CORS_ORIGIN (update after Vercel deploy)
- [ ] Add ImageKit credentials (if using)
- [ ] Configure Redis (optional)
- [ ] Paste all into Render → Environment Variables
- [ ] Deploy backend
